@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - Prediction + PDF Download

actor User
participant Browser
participant FlaskAppController as Controller
participant AuthService as Auth
participant EncoderService as Encoder
participant ModelManager as Models
participant MetricsService as Metrics
participant ReportService as Report

User -> Browser: Open /login
Browser -> Controller: GET /login
Controller --> Browser: login page

User -> Browser: Submit login form
Browser -> Controller: POST /login
Controller -> Auth: validate_login(username,password)
Auth --> Controller: valid
Controller --> Browser: redirect /homepage

User -> Browser: Open prediction form
Browser -> Controller: GET /predict
Controller --> Browser: predict page (model options)

User -> Browser: Submit questionnaire + model_choice
Browser -> Controller: POST /predict
Controller -> Encoder: prepare_features(form_data)
Encoder --> Controller: encoded features + display features

Controller -> Models: predict(model_id, X)
Models --> Controller: prediction (0/1)
Controller -> Models: predict_proba(model_id, X)
Models --> Controller: confidence

Controller -> Metrics: metrics_by_model[model_id]
Metrics --> Controller: cm_plot + dist_plot + metrics
Controller --> Browser: result page (YES/NO + charts)

User -> Browser: Click Download PDF
Browser -> Controller: GET /download/pdf
Controller -> Metrics: metrics_by_model[model_id]
Metrics --> Controller: model metrics/charts
Controller -> Report: generate_pdf(assessment, metrics)
Report --> Controller: PDF bytes
Controller --> Browser: application/pdf download

@enduml
